menu "Watchdog Test"
    depends on RT_USING_WDT

config RT_UTEST_WDT
    bool "Watchdog Smoke Test"
    default n
    help
        Validate watchdog device find/open and timeout set/get. Optional
        start/keepalive/stop is off by default to avoid board reset when the
        hardware cannot stop the WDT.

if RT_UTEST_WDT

    config RT_UTEST_WDT_DEVICE_NAME
        string "Watchdog Device Name"
        default "wdt"
        help
            Device name registered by the BSP, usually "wdt".

    config RT_UTEST_WDT_TIMEOUT_SEC
        int "Timeout Used by Smoke Test (Seconds)"
        range 1 60
        default 5
        help
            Timeout value written by SET_TIMEOUT and checked by GET_TIMEOUT.
            The value read back may differ by up to
            RT_UTEST_WDT_TIMEOUT_TOL seconds because watchdog timeouts are
            derived from a divided low-speed clock (e.g. STM32 LSI 32kHz).

    config RT_UTEST_WDT_TIMEOUT_TOL
        int "Accepted Readback Tolerance (Seconds)"
        range 0 5
        default 1
        help
            Absolute tolerance between the programmed timeout and the value
            read back through GET_TIMEOUT. 0 requires an exact round-trip.

    config RT_UTEST_WDT_STOPPABLE
        bool "Watchdog Can Be Stopped (RT_DEVICE_CTRL_WDT_STOP)"
        default n
        help
            Some watchdog blocks (e.g. STM32 IWDG) cannot be stopped at all.
            rt_device_close() on a watchdog issues RT_DEVICE_CTRL_WDT_STOP and
            fails with -RT_ERROR when the driver has no STOP support, which
            would also leave the device reference count incremented and break
            a second run of this suite.

            With this option disabled (default) the test never closes the
            device: it is a hardware-global singleton, so the handle is only
            released by the test case and a re-run reuses the already opened
            device. Enable it on BSPs whose watchdog really supports STOP to
            exercise the close path.

    config RT_UTEST_WDT_START
        bool "Also Start/Keepalive/Stop Watchdog"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, the test starts the WDT with the configured timeout,
            feeds it once, then stops it. Keep this off unless the BSP WDT can
            be stopped safely; otherwise the board may reset if STOP fails.

endif

endmenu
